What is here
  A subset of the release, files copied byte for byte with no edits:
    COPYING README AUTHORS NEWS LZO.lsm
    include/lzoconf.h include/lzo1x.h
    src/lzo1x_1.c src/lzo1x_d1.c src/config1x.h src/lzo_conf.h
    src/lzo_util.h src/lzo_dict.h src/lzo_ptr.h
    src/lzo1x_c.ch src/lzo1x_d.ch src/lzo1_d.ch
  Only the files these two sources include are kept; the rest of the
  release (other algorithms, minilzo, examples, build scripts) is omitted.

Modifications (gagarin, 2026)
  No source file is changed. The build configuration differs from the
  upstream defaults, set only by compiler flags in match/lib/lzo/lzo1x.c:
    /Gr /D__LZO_ENTRY=          public entry points use __fastcall
    /U_M_IX86                   no i386 unaligned-access paths
    /Dlzo_moff_t=lzo_ptrdiff_t  signed match offsets (selects the #else branch
    /Dlzo_cmoff_t=lzo_ptrdiff_t of the lzo_moff_t switch in src/lzo_conf.h)
  and match/lib/lzo/lzo1x.c compiles lzo1x_1.c and the decoder as one
  translation unit.

Decoder reconstruction
  The decoder is NOT the vendored lzo1x_d1.c. The LZO version that produced
  the shipped decoder is unrecoverable (1.01 and 1.02 are not archived), and
  neither 1.00 nor 1.03 reproduces it. match/lib/lzo/lzo1x_decompress_ww.inc is a
  gagarin reconstruction derived from LZO 1.00's src/lzo1x_d.ch (GPL-2.0-or-later,
  used here under GPL-3.0-or-later); it keeps 1.00's algorithm and structure and
  differs from it as follows (all taken from the shipped code, not from a later
  release):
    - no overrun/lookbehind checks, no byte-order or alignment paths;
    - the literal-run length is built as 15 (31, 7 for M3, M4) plus the zero
      bytes plus the final byte, rather than "t += 15 + *ip++";
    - the initial-literal copy shares the literal-run copy loop;
    - the match chain has no M1 case; M1 is handled after the literal copy;
    - the return is two-way (0 if all input was consumed, else -1).
  LZO 1.03 (not vendored) was compared: its decoder adds "if (t < 4) goto
  match_next" after the initial literals and preset-dictionary support, which
  the shipped code lacks, so the reconstruction follows 1.00. The vendored
  lzo1x_d1.c/lzo1x_d.ch stay in the tree unmodified but are no longer compiled.
